# W44-216 partial-corpus MLP smoke fit
# Run on partial fleet output (1511 of 25480 target cells, ~6%).
# Wall-time: fleet ran ~17 min on 9 → 7 pods before this snapshot.
# Inputs: /tmp/w44-216-cells/*.parquet → /tmp/w44-216-merged-early/merged.parquet
#
# Hypothesis: RuntimeTuning params (the W44-213 wired struct) actually
# affect encoded output bytes — i.e. the wiring is plumbed end-to-end
# correctly and the params have measurable response in the cost model.
#
# Result: R^2 = 0.8409 (well above the 0.7 threshold).
# All 6 RuntimeTuning params are statistically responsive
# (permutation importance > 0.001 each).
# Top-responding param: adaptive_quant_screenshot_qf_seed_scale_e7
# (importance 0.153 ± 0.023).
#
# This confirms the W44-216 fleet infrastructure produces useful
# training data; the full 25K+ cell run will give the MLP enough
# resolution per (image, effort, distance, strategy) cell to learn
# the local response surface for Bayesian-opt seeding.
#
# Provenance:
#   commit_sha: ad639aa86782355552ca0d2464b102a0f60cc8d3
#   sweep_id: w44-216-stage-b
#   bucket: s3://zen-tuning-ephemeral/w44-216-stage-b/cells/
#   image: ghcr.io/lilith/zenjxl-tuning-sweep:v2-w44-216
